# Companio — Docker build context excludes (Phase 11)
#
# Applies to `docker build` invocations run from the repo root (both
# apps/api/Dockerfile and apps/web/Dockerfile expect that build context —
# see docker-compose.prod.yml). Keeps the build context small and, most
# importantly, makes sure nothing secret or unnecessary ever gets copied
# into an image layer.

# Secrets — SECURITY.md §7 promises these are "never baked into a Docker
# image layer". Real values only ever reach containers via environment
# variables / a secrets manager at run time, never COPYed in at build time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json, not
# copied from the host (host node_modules may contain host-platform native
# binaries that don't match the image's architecture/libc).
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — rebuilt inside the image. Stale host builds (e.g. a local
# apps/web/.next from `npm run dev`) must never leak into an image layer.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
build
**/build

# Version control / editor / OS cruft
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test / coverage / load-test artifacts — not part of a runtime image
coverage
**/coverage
loadtest
scripts

# Docs — large, frequently-edited, irrelevant to what actually runs
*.md

# Local dev compose files (the prod compose file explicitly excludes
# itself too, so editing it doesn't invalidate every build's cache)
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml

# Misc
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
*.log
